The learned component in this thesis is a masked finite-horizon candidate-value function: it predicts #symb.rl.qh values for a finite candidate table, and the decision rule selects among hard-valid rows. Training evidence is generated by offline, mesh-supervised counterfactual replay. @aria-synthetic-environments:short contributes both sensor-like logged streams and privileged ground truth; @egocentric-foundation-model-3d:short converts the logged subset into a local 3D representation, whereas depth, segmentation, @ground-truth:short boxes, meshes, counterfactual renders, and reconstruction labels remain supervision or evaluation channels @ProjectAria-ASE-2025 @EFM3D-straub2024. Storage in the same adapted snippet does not make these channels equally observable.

